---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Input Sigil — Portfolio">
  <article class="sigil-page">
    <header class="sigil-page__header">
      <p class="eyebrow">Web development / interface specimen</p>
      <h1 aria-label="[ PROVENANCE / 00.1 ] INPUT SIGIL">
        <span class="sigil-page__stamp"><span data-sigil-stamp aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="sigil-page__cursor" data-sigil-stamp-cursor aria-hidden="true"></span></span>
        <span class="sigil-page__title"><span data-sigil-title aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="sigil-page__cursor is-hidden" data-sigil-title-cursor aria-hidden="true"></span></span>
      </h1>
      <p class="sigil-page__summary">
        A familiar input control from an adjacent machine. <br> One button, 216 living bits, and a small argument with certainty. <br> Now listening to <span class="sigil-page__location" aria-label="Rovinj, Istria"><span data-sigil-location aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="sigil-page__location-cursor" aria-hidden="true"></span></span>.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="specimen" aria-labelledby="specimen-title">
      <div class="specimen__stage">
        <p class="eyebrow">Completed specimen / local signal</p>
        <button class="sigil" type="button" aria-label="Input specimen">
          <span class="sigil__background" data-sigil-background aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span class="sigil__bits" data-sigil-bits aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span class="sigil__line"><span class="sigil__input"><span data-sigil-input aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="sigil__cursor" aria-hidden="true"></span></span><span class="sigil__local">00 // LOCAL</span></span>
        </button>
      </div>
      <div class="specimen__copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">The object</p>
        <h2 id="specimen-title">It looks like a button until it starts remembering.</h2>
        <p>
          Input Sigil is a small interface organism made for Proof Sheet. It accepts one familiar command—input—and
          gives it a chassis, a living screen, a memory of local machines, and just enough electrical instability to
          make the familiar feel newly discovered.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="anatomy" aria-labelledby="anatomy-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">Disassembly / 00 → 04</p>
      <h2 id="anatomy-title">The button is five small machines pretending to be one.</h2>
      <ol class="anatomy__list">
        <li>
          <span class="anatomy__number">00</span>
          <div><span class="part-specimen part-chassis" aria-hidden="true"><span></span></span><h3>The chassis</h3><p>A dark, raised analog shell gives the control physical mass: inset rim, painted edge, contact shadow, and a small pressed state. The object begins as something the hand already understands.</p></div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="anatomy__number">01</span>
          <div><span class="part-specimen part-field part-field--background" data-sigil-part-background aria-hidden="true"></span><h3>The substrate</h3><p>The background is no longer a decorative texture. It is 216 individual orange bits arranged in a continuous 24×9 field. Each cell is a possible mark, not a piece of a finished picture.</p></div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="anatomy__number">02</span>
          <div><span class="part-specimen part-field part-field--signal" data-sigil-part-signal aria-hidden="true"></span><h3>The signal</h3><p>The upper field is 108 white one-bit cells in a 36×3 strip. Every bit makes its own decision once per second, after its own delay. The field never redraws as one obedient rectangle; shapes arrive as a side effect of disagreement.</p></div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="anatomy__number">03</span>
          <div><span class="part-specimen part-power" data-sigil-part-power aria-hidden="true"><b>INPUT</b><b>00 // LOCAL</b></span><h3>The power event</h3><p>INPUT, 00 // LOCAL, and the perimeter aura share one slow, irregular surge. Their brightness, opacity, and glow rise and fall together like one screen on unstable current.</p></div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="anatomy__number">04</span>
          <div><span class="part-specimen part-terminal" aria-hidden="true"><span data-sigil-part-input></span><i></i></span><h3>The incantation</h3><p>INPUT types itself into existence. The block cursor stays behind, flashing in the old terminal rhythm, waiting for the next command. The label is not decoration; it is the machine speaking its command aloud.</p></div>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="logic" aria-labelledby="logic-title">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Runtime / no illusion of stillness</p>
        <h2 id="logic-title">The magic is only timing.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="logic__signal" aria-hidden="true"><span data-sigil-logic-signal></span></div>
      <div class="logic__text">
        <p>
          A 24×9 field underneath, a 36×3 strip above it / 324 bits in all. Each one wakes on its own private delay, then decides again every second, alone, forever. Nothing here loops. Nothing here is told what to become. The image is only what a crowd looks like when no one is in charge of it.
        </p>
        <p>
          The text doesn't get to disagree with itself. It belongs to one machine, so it keeps one clock / a slow surge in brightness and glow, shared by both labels, in lockstep. Right now that clock is quietly listening to Rovinj, Istria. Weather it has never seen is deciding how fast a light breathes here. Familiar enough to read. Unfamiliar enough to feel alive.
        </p>
        <p>
          The signal didn't stay inside the button. A vertical field runs beside this paragraph now, and a ring of three-bit decisions circles the next idea before you've read it. The same small choice can be a pixel, a border, a reply to the weather, or the edge of a thought. Its shape changes. What's deciding it doesn't.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="potential" aria-labelledby="potential-title">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Potential / the next signal</p>
        <div class="potential__heading">
          <span class="potential__ring" data-sigil-potential-ring aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <h2 id="potential-title">What else could leave a trace?</h2>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="potential__text">
        <p>
          This one remembers almost nothing / a seed, a place, an hour. A real provenance runs longer than that: every hand, every condition, every decision that had to happen for this exact object to exist. The button could hold more of that chain.
        </p>
        <ol class="potential__list">
          <li><span>08</span><strong>Inheritance</strong><p>Every state could carry its parents forward / the image, the weather, the seed, the model, the hand that pressed it. Not a certificate stapled on after the fact. Proof folded into the object at the moment it became itself.</p></li>
          <li><span>09</span><strong>Unresolved</strong><p>Most chains break somewhere. Rather than inventing the missing link, the object could just show the break / a dark interval, an orbit with nothing in it, a field that never quite resolves. Not knowing, rendered honestly, is still information.</p></li>
          <li><span>10</span><strong>Conservation</strong><p>Everything this runs on will eventually be gone / the browser, the font, the machine reading this sentence. Before that happens, the sigil could leave behind what it would take to meet it again: its seed, its conditions, its dependencies, in order. Not a photograph of the thing. A way back to it.</p></li>
          <li><span>11</span><strong>Borrowed Light</strong><p>Not every decision in the object is its own. Weather, the clock, a model version upstream / all of it leaves fingerprints the object didn't choose. It could mark which parts of itself are borrowed, and from where.</p></li>
          <li><span>12</span><strong>Silent Revision</strong><p>Something changed and nothing announced it. The object could hold the version it remembers being next to the version it currently is, and refuse to quietly reconcile the two.</p></li>
          <li><span>13</span><strong>Refusal</strong><p>Most systems default to a confident guess when they don't know. This one could have a state that means exactly I won't claim to know that / distinct from wrong, distinct from missing.</p></li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="specs" aria-labelledby="specs-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">Field notes</p>
      <h2 id="specs-title">A small control with a suspicious amount of interior life.</h2>
      <dl>
        <div><dt>Bits</dt><dd>216 total / 108 orange / 108 white</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Pattern</dt><dd>24×9 background substrate / 36×3 signal strip</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Cadence</dt><dd>One independent state decision per second</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Power</dt><dd>One shared, eased surge cycle biased by Rovinj conditions</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Runtime</dt><dd>Plain HTML, CSS, and JavaScript</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Weather source</dt><dd>Rovinj, Istria / current conditions</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Fallback</dt><dd>Weather failure and reduced motion preserve the local specimen</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </section>
  </article>
</Base>

<script>
  const initSigilPage = () => {
    const stamp = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-sigil-stamp]');
    const title = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-sigil-title]');
    const stampCursor = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-sigil-stamp-cursor]');
    const titleCursor = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-sigil-title-cursor]');
    const background = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-sigil-background]');
    const bits = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-sigil-bits]');
    const input = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-sigil-input]');
    const partBackground = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-sigil-part-background]');
    const partSignal = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-sigil-part-signal]');
    const partPower = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-sigil-part-power]');
    const partInput = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-sigil-part-input]');
    const logicSignal = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-sigil-logic-signal]');
    const logicText = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.logic__text');
    const potentialRing = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-sigil-potential-ring]');
    const location = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-sigil-location]');
    const line = input?.closest<HTMLElement>('.sigil__line');
    const button = input?.closest<HTMLElement>('.sigil');
    if (!stamp || !title || !stampCursor || !titleCursor || !background || !bits || !input || !line || !button || stamp.dataset.ready) return;
    stamp.dataset.ready = 'true';
    const flickerDuration = `${(14 + Math.random() * 10).toFixed(2)}s`;
    const flickerDelay = `${(-Math.random() * 5).toFixed(2)}s`;
    line.style.setProperty('--flicker-duration', flickerDuration);
    line.style.setProperty('--flicker-delay', flickerDelay);
    button.style.setProperty('--flicker-duration', flickerDuration);
    button.style.setProperty('--flicker-delay', flickerDelay);
    stamp.style.setProperty('--flicker-duration', flickerDuration);
    stamp.style.setProperty('--flicker-delay', flickerDelay);
    title.style.setProperty('--flicker-duration', flickerDuration);
    title.style.setProperty('--flicker-delay', flickerDelay);
    partPower?.style.setProperty('--flicker-duration', flickerDuration);
    partPower?.style.setProperty('--flicker-delay', flickerDelay);
    const reducedMotion = window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;
    let weatherBias = 0;
    const randomizeBit = (bit: HTMLElement) => bit.classList.toggle('is-on', Math.random() > (.48 - weatherBias));
    const scheduleBit = (bit: HTMLElement) => {
      if (reducedMotion) return;
      window.setTimeout(() => window.setInterval(() => randomizeBit(bit), 1000), Math.random() * 1000);
    };
    const addField = (field: HTMLElement, flicker: boolean, count: number) => {
      for (let index = 0; index < count; index += 1) {
        const bit = document.createElement('b');
        randomizeBit(bit);
        field.append(bit);
        scheduleBit(bit);
        if (flicker) {
          bit.style.setProperty('--bit-duration', `${(2.1 + Math.random() * 3.8).toFixed(2)}s`);
          bit.style.setProperty('--bit-delay', `${(-Math.random() * 5.8).toFixed(2)}s`);
        }
      }
    };
    addField(background, false, 216);
    addField(bits, true, 108);
    if (partBackground) addField(partBackground, false, 72);
    if (partSignal) addField(partSignal, true, 108);
    if (logicSignal) {
      const rows = Math.max(36, Math.ceil((logicText?.getBoundingClientRect().height ?? 179) / 5));
      logicSignal.style.setProperty('--logic-rows', String(rows));
      logicSignal.style.setProperty('--logic-height', `${(rows * 5) - 1}px`);
      addField(logicSignal, true, rows * 3);
    }
    if (potentialRing) {
      const ringBounds = potentialRing.getBoundingClientRect();
      const ringRadius = Math.max(72, (Math.max(ringBounds.width, ringBounds.height) / 2) - 4);
      const ringPoints = 216;
      for (let index = 0; index < ringPoints; index += 1) {
        const angle = index * (360 / ringPoints);
        const radians = (angle * Math.PI) / 180;
        const holder = document.createElement('i');
        holder.style.left = `calc(50% + ${(Math.cos(radians) * ringRadius).toFixed(2)}px)`;
        holder.style.top = `calc(50% + ${(Math.sin(radians) * ringRadius).toFixed(2)}px)`;
        holder.style.transform = `rotate(${angle}deg)`;
        for (let width = 0; width < 3; width += 1) {
          const bit = document.createElement('b');
          randomizeBit(bit);
          bit.style.setProperty('--bit-duration', `${(2.1 + Math.random() * 3.8).toFixed(2)}s`);
          bit.style.setProperty('--bit-delay', `${(-Math.random() * 5.8).toFixed(2)}s`);
          holder.append(bit);
          scheduleBit(bit);
        }
        potentialRing.append(holder);
      }
    }
    let typingDelay = 240;
    const type = (target: HTMLElement, text: string, done: () => void) => {
      let index = 0;
      const typeNext = () => {
        target.textContent = text.slice(0, index);
        index += 1;
        if (index <= text.length) {
          const variation = typingDelay * ((Math.random() * .7) - .35);
          window.setTimeout(typeNext, Math.max(75, typingDelay + variation));
        }
        else done();
      };
      typeNext();
    };
    if (reducedMotion) {
      stamp.textContent = '[ PROVENANCE / 00.1 ]';
      title.textContent = 'INPUT SIGIL';
      input.textContent = 'INPUT';
      if (partInput) partInput.textContent = 'INPUT';
      if (location) location.textContent = 'Rovinj, Istria';
      stampCursor.classList.add('is-hidden');
      titleCursor.classList.remove('is-hidden');
      return;
    }
    window.setTimeout(() => type(stamp, '[ PROVENANCE / 00.1 ]', () => window.setTimeout(() => {
      stampCursor.classList.add('is-hidden');
      titleCursor.classList.remove('is-hidden');
      type(title, 'INPUT SIGIL', () => undefined);
    }, 180)), 420);
    window.setTimeout(() => type(input, 'INPUT', () => undefined), 900);
    if (partInput) {
      const repeatType = () => type(partInput, 'INPUT', () => window.setTimeout(repeatType, 10000));
      window.setTimeout(repeatType, 1100);
    }
    if (location) window.setTimeout(() => type(location, 'Rovinj, Istria', () => undefined), 1500);

    const applyRovinjWeather = async () => {
      try {
        const response = await fetch('https://api.open-meteo.com/v1/forecast?latitude=45.0812&longitude=13.6387&current=precipitation,wind_speed_10m,cloud_cover,weather_code&timezone=Europe%2FZagreb');
        if (!response.ok) return;
        const payload = await response.json() as { current?: { precipitation?: number; wind_speed_10m?: number; cloud_cover?: number; weather_code?: number } };
        const current = payload.current;
        if (!current) return;
        const activity = Math.min(1, ((current.precipitation ?? 0) * .12) + ((current.wind_speed_10m ?? 0) * .006) + ((current.cloud_cover ?? 0) * .0015) + ((current.weather_code ?? 0) >= 51 ? .08 : 0));
        weatherBias = activity * .12;
        typingDelay = 210 + (activity * 150);
        const duration = `${(14 + ((1 - activity) * 10)).toFixed(2)}s`;
        line.style.setProperty('--flicker-duration', duration);
        button.style.setProperty('--flicker-duration', duration);
        partPower?.style.setProperty('--flicker-duration', duration);
      } catch {
        // Local randomness remains the fallback when weather is unavailable.
      }
    };
    void applyRovinjWeather();
  };
  initSigilPage();
  document.addEventListener('astro:page-load', initSigilPage);
</script>

<style>
  .sigil-page { max-width: 90rem; min-width: 0; margin-inline: auto; padding-top: clamp(3rem, 10vw, 8rem); }
  .sigil-page__header { max-width: 64rem; }
  .eyebrow { font-size: .8rem; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  h1 { display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; margin-block: 1rem; font-size: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 7rem); line-height: .85; letter-spacing: -.07em; font-weight: 400; }
  h2 { max-width: 15ch; margin-block: .75rem 1.5rem; font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 6vw, 5.5rem); line-height: .95; }
  .sigil-page__stamp { display: inline-flex; align-items: baseline; margin-bottom: .7em; color: var(--earthsong-orange); font-size: .18em; line-height: 1; letter-spacing: .08em; animation: sigil-title-flicker var(--flicker-duration,18s) ease-in-out infinite var(--flicker-delay,0s); }
  .sigil-page__title { display: inline-flex; align-items: baseline; animation: sigil-title-flicker var(--flicker-duration,18s) ease-in-out infinite var(--flicker-delay,0s); }
  .sigil-page__cursor, .sigil__cursor { display: inline-block; width: .55ch; height: .78em; margin-left: .14ch; vertical-align: -.04em; background: currentColor; animation: sigil-cursor 1s steps(1, end) infinite; }
  .sigil-page__cursor.is-hidden { display: none; }
  .sigil-page__summary { max-width: 43rem; font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 3vw, 2rem); }
  .sigil-page__location { display: inline-flex; align-items: baseline; }
  .sigil-page__location-cursor { display: inline-block; width: .55ch; height: .78em; margin-left: .1ch; vertical-align: -.08em; background: currentColor; animation: sigil-cursor 1s steps(1, end) infinite; }
  .specimen { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(18rem, .8fr) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: clamp(2rem, 8vw, 8rem); align-items: center; margin-top: clamp(5rem, 12vw, 10rem); padding-block: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem); border-block: 1px solid currentColor; }
  .specimen__stage { min-height: 17rem; display: grid; align-content: center; justify-items: start; padding: clamp(1.5rem, 5vw, 4rem); background: #211f1c; border: 1px solid var(--earthsong-muted); }
  .specimen__stage .eyebrow { margin-top: 0; }
  .sigil { position: relative; isolation: isolate; display: inline-flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: stretch; justify-content: flex-start; gap: .2rem; appearance: none; min-width: 13rem; min-height: 6rem; padding: .7rem .8rem .65rem; border: 2px solid var(--earthsong-orange); border-radius: .15rem; background: #080a07; color: #e5c6a8; text-align: left; font: inherit; letter-spacing: .06em; cursor: pointer; width: max-content; box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px #111, inset 0 0 18px rgba(255,145,104,.08), 0 0 0 1px #050605, 0 5px 0 #050605, 0 8px 14px rgba(0,0,0,.45); transition: transform 80ms ease, box-shadow 80ms ease, filter 80ms ease; }
  .sigil::before { content: ''; position: absolute; z-index: -1; inset: .25rem; border: 1px solid rgba(229,198,168,.45); pointer-events: none; }
  .sigil::after { content: ''; position: absolute; z-index: -1; inset: -.3rem; border: 1px solid var(--earthsong-orange); border-radius: .35rem; background: transparent; opacity: .38; filter: blur(7px); box-shadow: 0 0 18px rgba(255,145,104,.9), 0 0 42px rgba(255,145,104,.52); pointer-events: none; animation: sigil-screen-aura var(--flicker-duration,18s) ease-in-out infinite var(--flicker-delay,0s); }
  .sigil__background { position: absolute; z-index: 0; inset: .7rem; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(24, 1fr); grid-template-rows: repeat(9, 1fr); gap: 0; opacity: .32; pointer-events: none; }
  .sigil__bits { position: relative; z-index: 1; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(36, 4px); grid-template-rows: repeat(3, 4px); gap: 1px; min-height: 1.3rem; pointer-events: none; }
  .sigil__background :global(b) { display: block; width: auto; height: auto; background: transparent; }
  .sigil__bits :global(b) { display: block; width: 4px; height: 4px; background: transparent; }
  .sigil__background :global(b.is-on) { background: var(--earthsong-orange); box-shadow: 0 0 3px rgba(255,145,104,.8); }
  .sigil__bits { z-index: 1; gap: 1px; color: #fff7ea; filter: contrast(1.8); text-shadow: 0 0 8px rgba(255,247,234,.95), 0 0 18px rgba(255,247,234,.9), 0 0 32px rgba(255,247,234,.78), 0 0 50px rgba(255,247,234,.58); }
  .sigil__bits :global(b.is-on) { background: currentColor; box-shadow: 0 0 3px currentColor, 0 0 9px currentColor, 0 0 18px rgba(255,247,234,.95), 0 0 34px rgba(255,247,234,.75); animation: sigil-bit-flicker var(--bit-duration,3.6s) ease-in-out infinite var(--bit-delay,0s); }
  .sigil__line { position: relative; z-index: 1; display: flex; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; padding-top: .45rem; border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,145,104,.45); font-size: .78rem; letter-spacing: .08em; }
  .sigil__input { display: inline-flex; align-items: baseline; font-weight: 700; text-shadow: 0 0 4px rgba(229,198,168,.9), 0 0 10px rgba(229,198,168,.72), 0 0 20px rgba(229,198,168,.5), 0 0 34px rgba(229,198,168,.32); animation: sigil-power var(--flicker-duration,18s) ease-in-out infinite var(--flicker-delay,0s); }
  .sigil__local { color: var(--earthsong-orange); font-size: .52rem; line-height: 1; letter-spacing: .12em; font-weight: 700; text-shadow: 0 0 4px rgba(255,145,104,.95), 0 0 10px rgba(255,145,104,.78), 0 0 20px rgba(255,145,104,.56), 0 0 34px rgba(255,145,104,.36); animation: sigil-power var(--flicker-duration,19s) ease-in-out infinite var(--flicker-delay,-1.7s); }
  .sigil__cursor { width: .55ch; height: .82em; margin-left: .1ch; vertical-align: -.08em; background: currentColor; animation: sigil-cursor 1s steps(1, end) infinite; }
  .specimen__copy { max-width: 42rem; }
  .anatomy, .logic, .specs { margin-top: clamp(6rem, 14vw, 12rem); }
  .anatomy__list { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(5, 1fr); gap: 1px; margin: 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; border-block: 1px solid currentColor; }
  .anatomy__list li { min-height: 18rem; padding: 1.25rem 1rem 1.5rem 0; }
  .anatomy__list li + li { padding-left: 1rem; border-left: 1px solid currentColor; }
  .anatomy__number { color: var(--earthsong-orange); font-size: .75rem; letter-spacing: .1em; }
  .part-specimen { display: block; width: 100%; height: 5.4rem; margin: 1.5rem 0 2rem; overflow: hidden; }
  .part-chassis { position: relative; border: 2px solid var(--earthsong-orange); border-radius: .15rem; background: #080a07; box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px #111, inset 0 0 18px rgba(255,145,104,.08), 0 0 0 1px #050605, 0 5px 0 #050605, 0 8px 14px rgba(0,0,0,.45); }
  .part-chassis::before { content: ''; position: absolute; inset: .3rem; border: 1px solid rgba(229,198,168,.45); }
  .part-chassis span { position: absolute; inset: .8rem 1rem; border: 1px solid rgba(255,145,104,.45); }
  .part-field { display: grid; gap: 0; padding: .7rem; background: #080a07; border: 1px solid var(--earthsong-orange); }
  .part-field--background { grid-template-columns: repeat(18, 1fr); grid-template-rows: repeat(4, 1fr); opacity: .9; }
  .part-field--signal { position: relative; grid-template-columns: repeat(36, 4px); grid-template-rows: repeat(3, 4px); align-content: center; justify-content: center; gap: 1px; width: 100%; height: 5.4rem; margin-bottom: 2rem; padding: 0; overflow: visible; border: 0; background: transparent; color: #fff7ea; filter: contrast(1.8); text-shadow: 0 0 8px rgba(255,247,234,.95), 0 0 18px rgba(255,247,234,.9), 0 0 32px rgba(255,247,234,.78), 0 0 50px rgba(255,247,234,.58); }
  .part-field :global(b) { display: block; min-width: 0; min-height: 0; background: transparent; }
  .part-field--background :global(b.is-on) { background: var(--earthsong-orange); box-shadow: 0 0 3px rgba(255,145,104,.8); }
